# Agent harness instructions (Claude / Codex). Local working context, not
# project content: they name the current work slice and cite paths under the
# private docs/internal/ tree. Root-anchored so a future per-directory
# CLAUDE.md stays trackable if one is ever wanted.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md

# heaptrack profiling artifacts
heaptrack.*.zst

# Editor swap/backup files. These mirror buffer contents verbatim, so a swap
# file for an ignored secret (.env.local) is itself a secret.
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# wiki repo (plain clone, not a submodule)
.wiki/

# Python build artifacts (generated by maturin develop / build.sh)
minigraf-ffi/python/minigraf/minigraf_ffi/
minigraf-ffi/python/**/__pycache__/
minigraf-ffi/python/.venv/
minigraf-ffi/python/dist/
.omc/
.serena/

# Third-party source trees kept locally for invariant comparison only.
# These are other projects' code — never commit them into this repository.
reference/

# Tool scratch output (graphify skill)
src/graphify-out/

# Caller-product internal documents (Vetch / Harrekki requirements, adoption
# plans, lane answers). These describe downstream products, not Vicia DB, and
# are deliberately kept out of this public repository. Tracked docs may cite
# paths under here; those citations only resolve in an internal checkout.
docs/internal/
